- **demo.py**: self-contained, standard library only, and it runs in under a second. It reproduces every exact value, checks additivity for degrees up to 210, and compares the split-channel formula with direct counts for $n = 3$ to $12$. It also runs a test on real primes below two million: type rates 0.1665 / 0.1666 / 0.3331 / 0.3338, and a pair-channel estimate of about 1.474.
